        "id": 1936647
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-04T20:58:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to the documentation:\n\n\"`map` transforms `Option\u003cT\u003e` to `Option\u003cU\u003e` by applying the provided function to the contained value of `Some` and leaving `None` values unchanged\"\n\nThe case I was trying to capture was if `device` was not found yielding `Err(())`. I think this does catch that, but I\u0027m realizing it will also return `Err(())` in the case that there had not been an existing value for the `property_type` key as `insert()` returns an option containing `None` or the previous value. This can be fixed, but to address your question: do we want to return a `Result` here or are we fine with this failing silently in the case the device does not exist?",
      "parentUuid": "b6a8bce9_820fff8a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 433,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 434,
        "endChar": 22
